 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Not necessarily, it's just slower going uphill. A mid drive helps a lot on those hills. Then wear gardening gloves, or at least a thick pair of fleece or fleece lined gloves. Cold hands stop you from enjoying the garden. That's a good idea. Snow plows every few stops, and heat pumps can fail. Yes, thin ski tires are worth having, they slip less on frozen surfaces. If you only have wide ones, narrow ones can be bought as cheap as a shop visit.",
